Blindness rationales:
  residue-certificate: SHEET (class data is 2-adic; conjugate for all odd b); DEFECT (a sparse planted defect changes no residue-class certificate density); UNIFORM (the certificate search is uniform over affine residue maps) [requires thin exceptional set]
  escape-induction: SHEET (escape lemmas at negated hostile points transfer to the other sheet); DRIFT (Applegate-Lagarias see-saw proves the 5x+1 analogue too (Caraiani 2010)); CHAIN (the A-L see-saw needs escape costs 1+2^(-j) -> 1; in E both base points cost >1 at every precision (v4)); DIRECTION (exclusion only) [requires thin exceptional set]
  density-drift: SHEET (function of parity words); DEFECT (measure-theoretic); INTEGRAL (rational cycles have measure zero); UNIFORM (drift sign is decidable)
  fourier-3adic: SHEET (Syrac_- = -Syrac_+ (inherited)); DEFECT (log-density statement); INTEGRAL (measure-theoretic); UNIFORM (applies to all 3n+b)
  linear-forms-logs: DRIFT (says nothing about unbounded orbits); DEFECT (blind to planted divergence)
  lp-difference-ineq: SHEET (inverse-tree counts are word functions); UNIFORM (LP systems exist for all 3n+b); DEFECT ((v4) gives counting lower bounds (about x^0.84 integers reach 1), never an every-orbit statement); DIRECTION (exclusion/counting only) [requires thin exceptional set]
  lyapunov-potential: none (placeholder)
  conjugacy-shift: SHEET (2-adic); DEFECT (measure); DRIFT (topological); INTEGRAL (all of Z_2); UNIFORM (all maps)
  finite-state-periodicity: SHEET (bounded orbits on both sheets are periodic); HARD ((v4) applies only to bounded orbits; growing orbits or chains are out of reach); DIRECTION (exclusion only) [requires thin exceptional set]
  transversality-proved: HARD (each excludes only a structured class: few digits, bounded p-adic closeness, end runs, balanced or Dio>eta words (transversality lane catalogue)); DRIFT (uniform over multiplicatively independent pairs (Theorem S holds for 5x+1 at alpha<0.804)); DIRECTION (exclusion only)
  transversality-hard: none (placeholder)
  periodic-approximant-liouville: HARD (reaches exactly the words with Dio(w) > eta(w) (Theorem D); HARD words have Dio <= eta); DRIFT (Theorem S holds for 5x+1 at alpha<0.804 and for Mahler's map); SHEET (holds for every 3x+r); DIRECTION (exclusion only)
  q-series-pade: HARD (needs a functional equation behind the word (square-swap words); cube-swap Y3 has none); DRIFT (Lemma P holds whenever mu_bar < phi, including some 5x+1 block words); DIRECTION (exclusion only)
  capacity-discrepancy: HARD (reaches only the critical slope: supercritical orbits grow exponentially and occupy density zero); SHEET (holds on 3n-1 in the stronger form (D8)); DIRECTION (exclusion only)
  forward-backward-duality: none
  choice-strategy: SHEET (relaxations are sheet-symmetric); DEFECT (residue-class based); DRIFT (E_5 exceptional mass -> 0 numerically; choice threshold q~10, not 4 (sibling ladder; Caraiani for the semigroup)) [requires thin exceptional set]
  order-pattern: DRIFT (ordinal patterns alone do not see growth rates); HARD ((v4) realized ordinal patterns are exactly the word-realizable ones (direction lemma); no exclusion of growing words); DIRECTION (exclusion only)
  carry-staircase: DRIFT (cycle-only); DEFECT (cycle-only); DIRECTION (exclusion only)
  functional-equation: DEFECT (encodes the map globally but proofs so far use growth heuristics)
  automata-rewriting: UNIFORM (a successful interpretation family would be a decidable criterion)
  measure-rigidity: DEFECT (measure statements); INTEGRAL (measure statements)
  sparse-verification: DRIFT (finite); DEFECT (finite); INTEGRAL (finite)

